    "result_text": "All clean. Both findings are addressed and the acceptance test remains green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Finding 1 \u2014 dead `sharesHousehold` plumbing (agreed, removed)\n\nSince the household-duplicate rejection was the only consumer of the flag, it was inert across all three layers. I removed it end-to-end for a coherent contract:\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 now calls `clinicService.createOwner(owner)`; dropped the `Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold())` computation.\n- **`ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 deleted the two-arg `createOwner(Owner, boolean)` overload and folded its body into the single `createOwner(Owner)`, so there's no longer a one-arg method delegating with a meaningless `false`.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 removed the `sharesHousehold` write-only property, and rewrote the now-inaccurate `householdId` description (it no longer depends on a flag; the id is always derived deterministically from last name + postcode). The generated DTO's `getSharesHousehold()` is gone, verified above.\n\n## Finding 2 \u2014 service\u2192mapper layering wrinkle (agreed, hoisted)\n\nI extracted the membership scoring into a standalone domain helper `MembershipLevels` (in the `service` package) with static `points(Owner)` and `level(Owner)` (the latter applies the stored cap). Now:\n\n- **`OwnerMapper`** delegates `membershipPoints`/`membershipLevel` to `MembershipLevels` (presentation \u2192 domain, the natural direction).\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl`** uses `MembershipLevels::level` directly and no longer injects `OwnerMapper` \u2014 the odd business-op-reaching-into-a-DTO-mapper dependency is gone, with no logic duplicated.\n\nI placed the helper in `service` rather than `model` deliberately: `MembershipLevels.points` depends on `RegistrationDateNormalizer` (in `rest.validation`), and the service layer already depends on that package, whereas putting it in `model` would have dragged a validation-layer dependency into the domain model \u2014 a worse inversion than the one being fixed.",
